# Everything below is OPTIONAL. The deployed site (stud-weld.vercel.app)
# works out of the box with no env vars set: the ChatGPT sign-in uses the
# device-code flow, and the AI chat is proxied through the bundled
# /api/codex Vercel serverless function. Only set these if you want to
# override the defaults (e.g. you registered your own OpenAI OAuth client
# so the OAuth redirect comes back to your own domain).

# --- Optional: override the Stud bridge URL (desktop / Roblox Studio plugin).
# Leave unset on Vercel — the web demo has no local Tauri bridge to talk to.
# VITE_STUD_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# --- Optional: use your own OpenAI OAuth client.
# OpenAI's public Codex client (app_EMoamEEZ73f0CkXaXp7hrann) has its
# redirect hardcoded to http://localhost:1455/auth/callback, so it cannot
# redirect back to a deployed website. If you register your own OAuth
# client at https://platform.openai.com/ and set BOTH of these to values
# whose registered redirect matches exactly, the OAuth redirect flow
# becomes available on the deployed domain. If you don't set these, the
# web app automatically uses the device-code sign-in flow (no redirect,
# works on any domain).
# VITE_CODEX_CLIENT_ID=app_your_client_id
# VITE_CODEX_REDIRECT_URI=https://stud-weld.vercel.app/auth/callback
